# Sonu-One Theme Development Rules

This repository contains specific guidelines and styling initiatives that must be followed when modifying or creating sections, blocks, templates, and styles.

---

## 1. Global Typography Settings Initiative (Sonu Typography)
To ensure absolute layout flexibility without bloating custom styles, all text selectors (headings, subheadings, role labels, body text, buttons) must support both **standard typography presets** and a **Custom** typography mode.

### Schema Requirements:
Every typography preset selector must use the following standard schema options:
```json
{
  "type": "select",
  "id": "heading_style",
  "label": "Heading Style",
  "options": [
    { "value": "h1", "label": "H1" },
    { "value": "h2", "label": "H2" },
    { "value": "h3", "label": "H3" },
    { "value": "h4", "label": "H4" },
    { "value": "h5", "label": "H5" },
    { "value": "h6", "label": "H6" },
    { "value": "p", "label": "Paragraph (P)" },
    { "value": "custom", "label": "Custom" }
  ],
  "default": "h2"
}
```

If a text element supports a typography preset selector, it **must** also include schema settings for individual properties prefixed with the selector's `id`:
```json
[
  {
    "type": "range",
    "id": "heading_style_font_size_desktop",
    "label": "Heading Custom Size (Desktop)",
    "min": 10,
    "max": 100,
    "step": 1,
    "unit": "px",
    "default": 32
  },
  {
    "type": "range",
    "id": "heading_style_font_size_mobile",
    "label": "Heading Custom Size (Mobile)",
    "min": 10,
    "max": 100,
    "step": 1,
    "unit": "px",
    "default": 24
  },
  {
    "type": "select",
    "id": "heading_style_font_weight",
    "label": "Heading Custom Font Weight",
    "options": [
      { "value": "300", "label": "Light" },
      { "value": "400", "label": "Regular" },
      { "value": "500", "label": "Medium" },
      { "value": "600", "label": "Semi-bold" },
      { "value": "700", "label": "Bold" }
    ],
    "default": "400"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "heading_style_line_height",
    "label": "Heading Custom Line Height",
    "default": "1.2"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "heading_style_letter_spacing",
    "label": "Heading Custom Letter Spacing (em / %)",
    "default": "0"
  },
  {
    "type": "select",
    "id": "heading_style_text_transform",
    "label": "Heading Custom Text Transform",
    "options": [
      { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
      { "value": "uppercase", "label": "Uppercase" },
      { "value": "lowercase", "label": "Lowercase" },
      { "value": "capitalize", "label": "Capitalize" }
    ],
    "default": "none"
  }
]
```

### Liquid Implementation:
1. Render custom typography style rules inline on the target HTML element using the `sonu-typography-style` snippet:
   ```html
   <h2 class="typography-{{ section.settings.heading_style | default: 'h2' }}" 
       style="{% render 'sonu-typography-style', preset: section.settings.heading_style, prefix: 'heading_style', settings: section.settings %}">
     {{ section.settings.heading }}
   </h2>
   ```
2. The `sonu-typography-style` snippet will output the corresponding CSS custom variables inline (e.g. `--custom-fs-desktop: 32px; --custom-fs-mobile: 24px; --custom-fw: 400;`), which are dynamically bound to the element by the global `.typography-custom` class in `css-variables.liquid`.

---

## 2. Text Highlight Parsing (`[[content]]` & `((content))`)
Always pass text content (especially headings, quotes, and testimonials) through highlight replacement filters to allow custom merchant-defined font highlights in the customizer.

*   `[[text]]`: Wraps the text in a serif/italic highlight class (e.g., `<span class="highlight">` or `<span class="sonu-highlight">` depending on layout context).
*   `((text))`: Wraps the text in secondary highlighted font styling (e.g., Times New Roman italic override `<span class="highlight-times">`).

### Liquid Parsing Examples:
*   Standard: `{{ text_val | replace: '[[', '<span class="highlight">' | replace: ']]', '</span>' }}`
*   Dual styles (e.g. `custom-step-slider-sh.liquid`):
    ```liquid
    assign formatted_heading = section.settings.heading 
      | replace: '[[', '<em class="highlight-pp">' | replace: ']]', '</em>' 
      | replace: '((', '<span class="highlight-times">' | replace: '))', '</span>'
    ```

---

## 3. Carousel Decoupling Initiative (Independent Swiping)
When constructing dual testimonials (left text, right video), **never** group a review card and a video inside a single slide wrapper. The text reviews grid and the portrait video slides must remain structurally decoupled so they can scroll independently.
*   Implement synchronized Swiper instances or separate navigations.
*   Always load Swiper via CDN UMD build (`swiper-bundle.min.js`) rather than local ES modules to avoid initialization script syntax errors in older environments.

---

## 4. Mobile Layout & Spacing Defaults
*   **Zero Side Gaps on Mobile Galleries**: For product image galleries on mobile, ensure images span full screen width with zero gaps by utilizing `aspect-ratio: 1` and `object-fit: cover` on images.
*   **Layout Shifts Prevention**: Always force `width: 100%` on hero slideshow containers to avoid right-side white space gaps on mobile browsers.
*   **Device-Specific Spacing Constraints**: Do not apply general margins/paddings that alter desktop balance. Spacing updates (such as spacing between subheadings and descriptions) should be wrapped in `@media` checks or mobile-specific schema ranges (e.g. `padding_bottom_mobile`).
